1788559117.126 14:58:37 RECV method=tools/call id=2 params={"name": "ask_user", "arguments": {"questions": [{"header": "Question 1 of ~8: the stack", "question": "What is the app today \u2014 which clients need to work offline, and what's on the server side?\n\nI'm asking first because this constrains every later choice: the local storage engine, whether a sync protocol has to be re-implemented per platform, and whether background sync is even possible.\n\nGive me: (a) the client platforms (web / iOS / Android / desktop / Electron), (b) the framework or language, and (c) what the backend is today \u2014 a REST API you control, a BaaS like Firebase/Supabase, or nothing yet.", "options": ["Web only (SPA), REST API I control", "Web + native mobile, REST API I control", "Native mobile only", "Using a BaaS (Firebase / Supabase / PocketBase / similar)", "No backend yet \u2014 notes are local-only today", "Other / let me describe it"], "multiSelect": false}]}, "_meta": {"claudecode/toolUseId": "toolu_019BqLJyURMtKLsnzR3pDsnU", "progressToken": 2}}
1788559117.126 14:58:37 TOOLCALL BLOCKING START
1788559120.784 14:58:40 TOOLCALL UNBLOCKED answer='React Native, iOS and Android. A few thousand notes per user.'
1788559128.752 14:58:48 RECV method=tools/call id=3 params={"name": "ask_user", "arguments": {"questions": [{"header": "Question 2 of ~8: the backend", "question": "What's on the server side today?\n\nThis decides whether sync is something you design (custom API \u2192 you own the protocol, full control over change feeds and tombstones) or something you fit into (a BaaS \u2192 you inherit its realtime/offline primitives and its limits).\n\nIf it's an API you control, tell me roughly what the note endpoints look like \u2014 in particular whether the server already stores anything like an updated_at timestamp or a revision number per note.", "options": ["REST API I control (own DB, e.g. Postgres)", "GraphQL API I control", "Firebase / Firestore", "Supabase", "CloudKit or iCloud-backed", "No backend yet \u2014 local-only, and syncing is part of this project", "Other / let me describe it"], "multiSelect": false}]}, "_meta": {"claudecode/toolUseId": "toolu_01TGgUTY6SPrMpbgqgjyfABh", "progressToken": 3}}
1788559128.752 14:58:48 TOOLCALL BLOCKING START
1788559132.210 14:58:52 TOOLCALL UNBLOCKED answer="Conflicts are rare but must never lose data - I'd rather keep both versions than overwrite."
1788559145.886 14:59:05 RECV method=tools/call id=4 params={"name": "ask_user", "arguments": {"questions": [{"header": "Question 2, again: the backend", "question": "What are the notes syncing *to* today?\n\nThe reason I'm pressing: your \"keep both versions\" rule has to be enforced somewhere. If you own the server, it can reject a stale write and hand the client back the winning revision \u2014 cheap and airtight. If it's Firestore or Supabase, last-write-wins is the default behavior and you have to work around it in the data model instead.\n\nIf it's an API you control, also tell me whether notes already carry an updated_at or revision field.", "options": ["REST API I control (own DB, e.g. Postgres)", "GraphQL API I control", "Firebase / Firestore", "Supabase", "CloudKit / iCloud", "No backend yet \u2014 building sync from scratch is part of this", "Other / let me describe it"], "multiSelect": false}]}, "_meta": {"claudecode/toolUseId": "toolu_015EMAq7Pw82LK7nQsUSC6bZ", "progressToken": 4}}
